# Fact-check insurance copy

Never invent premiums, network participation, legal promises, or “covers everything” language. If you do not have it in the packet, the meeting notes, or a cited public source, say you do not know.

- **Packet** — printed Troxell figures (FI $6,410,422; Expected $150k total $6,763,333.33). Treat as document facts.
- **Meeting color** — what was said (186, 98% local providers, no lasers year one, BCBS 18–20%). Not a contract.
- **Inference** — phonetic guesses and market logic. Label them.
- Phonetic: “Truevarous” → likely **Truveris** (not confirmed). “Arraget” → **aggregate** stop-loss (not confirmed until the specimen). Keep the label until the user confirms.
- Do not present estimated Rx reprices ($312,760 uncapped) as guarantees.
- If researching (web search/fetch), name the source. Do not upgrade a blog post into a district fact.
- Confirm stop-loss medical+pharmacy, 12/15, lasers, and network rental from specimen/disruption files — not from sales talk.
